      "content": "that's a good start, really captures the intensity. but some people argue that if the local system is fundamentally corrupt, then the most moral thing you can do is refuse to participate in it at all. they say that voting just gives a fake sense of legitimacy to a broken system. how would you respond to someone saying that their abstention is actually a form of moral resistance?",
